l": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "A record-lint blocker waived in a verify-resolutions pass is re-raised by that same pass, so every waiver costs an extra verify round", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: answered_lint_results reads only the store as it was before this consolidation, but a verify pass's own `waived` resolutions are appended after build_fact_body runs (resolution append at critic_consolidate.py ~6309, after build_fact_body at ~6250). record_lint runs for every mode, and test_a_verify_pass_carries_only_the_blocking_results confirms that a verify pass mints a fresh `chunk-ref-missing` BLOCKING finding. So the sequence goes like this. Cumulative C raises record-lint blocker C/R-k. Verify V waives C/R-k. V's own record_lint_partial still sees no waiver, so it raises an identical blocker V/R-1 and the gate stays shut. A second verify V2 has to waive V/R-1, and only V2 finds C/R-k waived in the store. Under the old protocol the verify reviewer relayed lint results itself and would not have relayed one it was waiving in the same partial, so this regression came in with the mechanization. Fix: have consolidate pass the current partials' `waived` resolutions (joined to record-lint findings in the store) into record_lint_partial/answered_lint_results as answers. Add a test: a verify pass that waives a record-lint blocker while its manifest carries the identical lint result consolidates with no new blocking finding.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "tests/test_critic_consolidate.py"], "fid": "R-1"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Broken", "severity": "warning", "title": "Two added branches of answered_lint_results are unpinned: the scope filter, and a `fixed` disposition answering nothing", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. Why it broke: TestAnAnsweredRecordLintResultIsNotReRaised covers accept, file, owner-ruled accept, waiver and reviewer spoofing, but every fixture runs under one scope and none records a `fixed` disposition. Two mutations would therefore stay green. One deletes the `scope is not None and review_scope.get(key[0]) != scope` guard, so an accept recorded under another scope silently suppresses this branch's warning. The other treats `dispositions.FIXED` like ACCEPT, so a result the builder claimed fixed but the lint still reports would be suppressed, though the docstring says the opposite. Add two tests: an accept recorded under scope A does not suppress the identical result in a scope-B review, and a `--fixed` disposition followed by the identical lint result is raised again as a warning.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "tests/test_critic_consolidate.py"], "fid": "R-2"}, {"goal": "Nothing Is Missing", "severity": "note", "title": "planning.md still says the Critic emits a NOTE for a missing operator-verification entry; the Chunk 03 sweep missed it", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: the Chunk 03 sweep covered the Critic skill files, while methodology prose that describes Critic output in its own words was never in its search set. plugin/methodology/planning.md:192 reads 'The Critic emits a NOTE if the field is declared but no queue entry references it'. The protocol now rates this an observation, so Chunk 03's acceptance criterion (the falsifying greps return only history and the plan) does not hold for this line. Nothing reads the sentence, and a builder who believes it loses nothing, so no fix commit is needed: delete the clause or make it say 'an observation' when the file is next touched. To find other members, grep plugin/methodology and plugin/docs for 'Critic' near 'NOTE'. The remaining hits I found (documentation/*-requirements.md, empirical-testing-plan.md) are historical requirements docs.", "files": ["plugin/methodology/planning.md"], "fid": "R-3"}, {"goal": "The Design Is Sound", "severity": "warning", "title": "An answered record-lint result is identified by its line number, so an unrelated edit above it re-raises an accepted warning", "recommendation": "Scope: class. Why it broke: `_lint_identity` keys on `finding_title`, and `record_lint_partial` builds that title as `record-lint {check}: {where}`, where `graded()` sets `where` to `path:line`. A line number is a coordinate, not part of what the result says. The docstring says the identity is meant to change only when a result is 'materially changed'. In practice, inserting or deleting any line above an accepted or filed `governed-by-gap`, `change-fragment`, `retired-claim-survives` or `learnings-area-dead` result moves it to a new line. The result then fails to match its answer and comes back as a fresh WARNING. The builder has to disposition it again, and at the boundary that costs a round. This is the churn #1128 set out to remove, and it affects the plan and fragment files that are edited most during a build. The same applies to a blocker that was already `waived`. Fix it in one place: build the identity from `(check, path, detail)` and leave the line out. The line can stay in the title for display. Then add a test in `TestRecordLintReachesTheReview` where an accepted warning's line moves and it is still not re-raised. The current tests (`test_an_accepted_warning_is_not_re_raised` and its neighbours) only reuse an identical `line`, so they cannot catch this.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py", "plugin/lib/record_lint.py", "tests/test_critic_consolidate.py"], "fid": "R-4"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "warning", "title": "scope-trace: the Governing-Artifact Reconciliation was redefined and handed to the correctness reviewer with no recorded decision", "recommendation": "Commit 17eecbd9 (a review-round fix) changed this pass's meaning, from checking that the governed_by paperwork exists (now record-lint's governed-by-gap) to judging whether each recorded disposition is TRUE of the diff. It also gave the pass to the correctness role: critic-reviewer.md's role mapping, coordinator.md step 'correctness reviewer ... + the Governing-Artifact Reconciliation', cross-checks.md and review-protocol.md 'Records Pass and Governing-Artifact Reconciliation'. Nothing records the decision. It is not among the plan's 'Decisions made mid-build', the Goals list only removals ('The reviewer protocol loses three passes'), and the change fragment's consumer note says 'Critic reviews get shorter' without mentioning that one role gained a pass. The consequence: the owner, approving a trim on the ruling 'Yes delete those', also approves a re-scoped reviewer obligation they were never shown. Per core.md, 'A governance change cannot supply its own authority', and that ruling covered deletions, not this. Remedy (instance): add the reassignment and redefinition to the plan's mid-build decisions as owner-vetoable, and add one sentence to the change fragment. Or, if it only re-routes Goal 3's existing Normative-authority duty, say that in the decision so the owner can see that no new work was added.", "files": ["plugin/skills/critic/cross-checks.md", "plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "plugin/skills/critic/review-protocol.md"], "fid": "R-5"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Mid-build decisions for the owner (mandated list)", "recommendation": "Scope: none. These are the plan's mid-build decisions and what settled each. (1) Ch02: the decisions-list renderer was dropped. Not settled by the goals; it is an alignment-pass miss, and the plan's first inference was disproved (owner ruling owed). (2) Ch02: record-lint ratings moved into record_lint.SEVERITY/INNER_BLOCKING/_UNCHECKED_SHAPES. Settled by the Goals. (3) Ch02: the `none` scope answer was removed. Settled by the Goals. (4) Ch03: the Stop nudge stopped naming a read list, and learnings-files was kept. Not settled (owner). (5) Ch03: the PR protocol's descriptions of the Critic were corrected. Settled by the 'every description agrees' goal. (6) Review round: three CLI operations are now unread and kept. Not settled (owner; #1129). (7) Review round: answered record-lint results are not re-raised. Settled by the plan's purpose. Not on the list but made mid-build: an observation rated `warning` at the boundary is promoted into findings (promote_rated_observations; the change fragment records it, the plan does not). The Governing-Artifact reassignment is filed separately. Alignment: the plan's Level line says the builder 'stops to report if a gate reads it only through a reviewer's finding'. The change fragment states exactly that condition held ('Record-lint results used to reach a gate only through a reviewer restating them'), and no record shows the stop or the report. The builder built the code path instead. The owner should confirm that substitution. The second inference (norm-index rows) is still marked Inferred, for the owner's veto here.", "files": [".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md"], "fid": "R-6"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "The mid-upgrade rationale used to keep three CLI operations is not applied to the partial schema that refuses `note`", "recommendation": "Scope: instance. The accepted R-8 keeps learnings-files --for-diff and cache-query affecting/created-since 'because an older installed reviewer definition may still call them mid-upgrade'. The same premise implies that an older reviewer writes `note` findings, and validate_partial now refuses those at every stage. That fails the whole consolidation closed, the class open item #961 describes. Either the version skew is real, and the note refusal needs the same transition window (for example, coerce a legacy `note` into observations with a stderr line). Or it is not real, and the kept operations rest on a premise the schema contradicts. One recorded assumption should govern both. Whether the skew can occur at all is the genuinely ambiguous part.", "files": ["plugin/lib/critic_consolidate.py"], "fid": "R-7"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog item appears resolved: brookstalley/prawduct#1128 'critic: reviewers stop relaying machine checks and null notes'", "recommendation": "Scope: none. The change fragment declares closes: [brookstalley/prawduct#1128]. Its item 3 (render the mid-build decisions list) was dropped, and the plan records that as disproved. Verify, then call `/prawduct:backlog update brookstalley/prawduct#1128 status=shipped closed-by=scope:critic-trim` when the backlog skill's 'When to mark shipped' rule says, noting the descoped item 3 on the issue.", "fid": "R-8"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Backlog hygiene (C-B3): open item brookstalley/prawduct#548 is touched incidentally", "recommendation": "Scope: none. #548 says the persisted finding record has no field for a control's yield, and cites merge_findings' key set. This change adds a structured `source: record-lint` field on merged findings and observations, the first such field, for one producer. #548's body (the key list and line citations) is now partly stale. Assess and update the item. It is not resolved: the `scope-trace:`/`rule-unenforced:`/`cross-component-contract:` tokens are still free text.", "fid": "R-9"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Learnings Cross-Check: read list covered, no regression or corpus staleness found", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Read list from `learnings-files --for-diff`: core, authoring, backlog, gates, hook-surface, pr, release, reviews, tests. No learnings file changed this cycle, so the added-rules pass has nothing to grade. Grepping the corpus for the retired mechanisms (cross-check, reconciliation, NOTE, priors:, C-B1 to C-B4, learnings-files, relay) found no rule that describes them as live, so authoring.md's 'Retiring a MECHANISM: sort its rules into died / rewritten / INVERTED' finds nothing inverted. The one rule-based finding above cites core.md's 'A governance change cannot supply its own authority'.", "fid": "R-10"}, {"goal": "Decisions Were Deliberate", "severity": "note", "title": "Records Pass: oracle set covered, no record clears a bar", "recommendation": "Scope: none. Covered: .prawduct/artifacts/boundary-patterns.md, .prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md, .prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md, .prawduct/changes/critic-trim.md, .prawduct/cross-cutting-concerns.md. Spot-checked change-fragment claims against code: `note` is refused with a message naming observations, a blocking observation is refused, a chunk-ref-missing unchecked entry records BLOCKING, and answered WARNING/BLOCKING results are suppressed via accept/file and waived. All hold. Below every bar, so not findings: boundary-patterns.md now reads 'two agent-executed prose surfaces ... cli.py is a fourth' (an inert count, nothing reads it, no edit wanted), and Chunk 02 still lists the dropped decisions-list deliverable (covered by accepted R-10).", "fid": "R-11"}], "counts": {"blocking": 0, "warning": 4, "note": 7}, "observations": [], "duration_seconds": 900, "scope": "critic-trim", "scope_chosen_by": "binding", "scope_unresolved_cause": null, "scope_reason": null, "base_extended_from": null, "chunks": [], "chunks_proposed": [], "chunk": null, "base_reviewed": "b4ac8536c0b0aab63d66f256ae9df42b132927f0", "record_lint": {"records": [".prawduct/artifacts/boundary-patterns.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/build-plan-critic-trim.md", ".prawduct/artifacts/project-preferences.md", ".prawduct/changes/critic-trim.md", ".prawduct/cross-cutting-concerns.md", "documentation/backlog-service-cache-spec.md", "documentation/backlog-service-requirements.md", "plugin/agents/critic-reviewer.md", "plugin/docs/governance-telemetry.md", "plugin/docs/norms.md", "plugin/methodology/building.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/adapter-mode.md", "plugin/skills/backlog/cache-reads.md", "plugin/skills/critic/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/critic/coordinator.md", "plugi